  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of circle of radius $\\sqrt{17}$ unit, with centre on the positive side of $x$ -axis and through the point $(0,1)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "RQuyC",
      "text": "$x^{2}+y^{2}-8 x-1=0$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "EvjUR",
      "text": "$x^{2}+y^{2}+8 x-1=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Hiu6d",
      "text": "$x^{2}+y^{2}-9 y+1=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "un4Kz",
      "text": "$2 x^{2}+2 y^{2}-3 x+2 y=4$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\nLet centre be $\\equiv(a, 0)(a>0)$\r\nSo, circle : $(x-a)^{2}+y^{2}=17 ;$ as it passes through $(0,1)$, so $a^{2}+1=17 \\quad \\Rightarrow a=4(a \\neq-4, a>0)$\r\n$\\therefore$ Equation is : $x^{2}+y^{2}-8 x-1=0$",
    "image": null
  },
